    "external": false,
    "title": "D&D Portal - How do you play a Bard?",
    "subTitle": "Bard FAQ",
    "description": "Play a Bard by using Charisma-based spellcasting, Bardic Inspiration, and strong skills to improve the party rather than focusing only on personal damage. Decide which enemies need controlling, which allies need support, and when an Inspiration die is worth spending. Your Bard College, spell choices, Expertise skills, and concentration management determine whether you lean toward support, control, social play, skill expertise, or martial combat.",
