    "external": false,
    "title": "D&D Portal - What ability scores are best for a Bard?",
    "subTitle": "Bard FAQ",
    "description": "Charisma is normally the Bard's highest ability score because it powers Bard spellcasting and Bardic Inspiration. Dexterity is usually the next priority because it improves Armor Class, initiative, Dexterity saving throws, and common finesse or ranged attacks. Constitution is also important for hit points and concentration. In the 2014 multiclassing rules, a Bard requires Charisma 13.",
